# Reverse-proxy configuration for the StupidChess web UI.
#
# `stupidchess serve` runs an HTTP server (static UI + JSON/SSE API) bound to localhost. It is exposed
# to the internet by Caddy, which terminates TLS and proxies to it, so the Go process is never directly
# reachable. Run the server as:
#
#     stupidchess serve --host 127.0.0.1 -p 8099
#
# (`--host 127.0.0.1` is the default; see deploy/stupidchess.service for the systemd unit.)
#
# It is hosted under a sub-path of an existing site, projects.ollybritton.com/stupidchess. The frontend
# resolves every request relative to the page (see serverURL() in static/app.js), so the `redir` to a
# trailing slash below is required: it makes the document base `/stupidchess/`, under which the stripped
# prefix lines up with the routes the Go server actually serves (`/`, `/api/*`, `/pieces/*`).
#
# Add this block inside the `https://projects.ollybritton.com { ... }` site:

redir /stupidchess /stupidchess/
handle_path /stupidchess/* {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8099
}

# Note on Server-Sent Events: the site's analytics snippet rewrites responses to inject a tracking
# script, which buffers the whole body and would stall the never-ending /api/events stream. Exclude the
# API from it by adding to the shared (analytics) snippet's response matcher:
#
#     @notjs {
#         not path_regexp notjs \.js$
#         not path /stupidchess/api/*
#     }
#
# Alternatively, host StupidChess on its own subdomain (https://stupidchess.ollybritton.com) with a
# plain `reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8099` and no analytics import; that avoids both the trailing-slash
# requirement and the SSE/analytics interaction entirely.
